# (id, what, old, new, k): single-point mutants of exp_smlm_real2.py (the second real-data pore study): the merged frames, the registration (rendering, correlation, shift curve,
# gate R1), the four ISS post-filters and their coordinate ascent, the choice of the configuration, the pore model of a test set, the reference events and the one-to-one matching
# of the overlap test, the counts and J_B, the equal-off-ring yield, the readings of the plan's rules A and B, the freeze hash and the bootstrap.
# Result: 65 mutants (Q01-Q65) and a control (Q00, passes). Against the first version of tests/test_exp_smlm_real2.py (41 tests) 12 survived (Q12, Q13, Q20, Q31, Q37, Q38, Q58-Q62:
# the polynomial degree of the shift curve, the frame-centre evaluation of the curve, the mean in place of the median amplitude, x_min inclusive, the border and the bright threshold of the
# reference events, the last block of the bootstrap, the pooled areas, the sign of the registration, the width scale of the continuity row, the 90th-percentile limit of gate R2); the tests
# added then (7: test_the_polynomial_degree..., test_shift_of_evaluates..., test_the_bootstrap_draws_every_block..., test_gate_r2_fails_on_the_ninetieth_percentile..., test_reg_loc_subtracts...,
# test_the_continuity_row_applies..., test_pooled_areas_are_summed...) and the sharpened ones kill 11 of them. ONE EQUIVALENT MUTANT: Q59 (the pooled areas not summed): the floor of the radial
# fit is b x (total area) with b = (floor counts)/(area), so a common factor on the area changes neither N, w nor the floor, and the pores of the members have the same radial area shape.
# Criterion: the tests file alone (pytest -x in a private copy of src/, experiments/ and tests/); the md regeneration was NOT run per mutant.
# Run: tools/mutants.py --exp exp_smlm_real2 --tests tests/test_exp_smlm_real2.py --raw results/smlm/real2_raw.npz --md results/smlm/real2.md --out-env REAL2_OUT
#      --spec tools/mutants/wp_smlmreal2_own.py --work <scratch dir> (the criterion is the tests file alone: the regeneration of the md takes tens of minutes per mutant and was NOT run)
# Wording round after the referee report A+B (the (void) reading mark, the transfer paragraph, the continuity row against the defaults, the grid-edge sentence): Q66-Q80 added (55 tests in all) and the anchor of Q56 updated to the
# present line of freeze_hash2. Criterion: the tests file alone, run with a tiny dummy raw (`--raw` a one-array npz named real2_raw.npz inside the repository, so that the md regeneration of the tool fails at once instead of taking
# 13 minutes per mutant). 15 of 15 killed; Q73 and Q74 (the 'beats' / 'worse' words read from the wrong end of an interval) first survived and are killed by the intervals that straddle 0 in
# test_the_transfer_paragraph_does_not_claim_a_reversal_or_a_win_the_numbers_do_not_show. Q56 is killed. The md was regenerated twice from the stored raw (byte identical, 13 minutes each).
